---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/resources/best-saas-appointment-setting-companies/"
title: "5 Best SaaS Appointment Setting Companies to Hire in 2027"
description: "Compare five SaaS appointment setting companies on pricing, buyer roles, demo qualification and sales handoff. See who fits your software sales team."
canonicalUrl: "https://www.callteam.ca/resources/best-saas-appointment-setting-companies/"
date: "2026-11-23"
modified: "2026-11-23"
contentLanguage: "en-CA"
ogType: "article"
pageStyles: ["/assets/css/lead-providers.css", "/assets/css/simple-buying-guide.css", "/assets/css/process-video-preview.css", "/assets/css/saas-appointment-shortlist.css"]
pageScripts: ["/assets/js/simple-buying-guide.js"]
---
{% set shortlist = saasAppointmentShortlist %}
{% from "components/process-video-preview.njk" import processVideoPreview %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[
  {"@type":"WebPage","@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#webpage","url":"{{ canonicalUrl }}","name":{{ title | json | safe }},"description":{{ description | json | safe }},"inLanguage":"en-CA","breadcrumb":{"@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#article"}},
  {"@type":"Article","@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#article","headline":{{ title | json | safe }},"description":{{ description | json | safe }},"datePublished":"{{ date | sitemapDate }}","dateModified":"{{ modified }}","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#webpage"},"author":{"@id":"{{ site.organizationId }}"},"publisher":{"@id":"{{ site.organizationId }}"}},
  {"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"{{ site.url }}/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Outbound Sales Library","item":"{{ site.url }}/resources/outbound-sales-library/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"SaaS appointment setting companies","item":"{{ canonicalUrl }}"}]},
  {"@type":"ItemList","@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#comparison","name":"SaaS appointment setting companies to hire in 2027","itemListOrder":"https://schema.org/ItemListUnordered","numberOfItems":{{ shortlist.providers | length }},"itemListElement":[{% for provider in shortlist.providers %}{"@type":"ListItem","position":{{ loop.index }},"name":{{ provider.name | json | safe }},"url":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#{{ provider.id }}"}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}]},
  {"@type":"FAQPage","@id":"{{ canonicalUrl }}#questions","mainEntity":[{% for faq in shortlist.faqs %}{"@type":"Question","name":{{ faq.question | json | safe }},"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":{{ faq.answer | json | safe }}}}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}]}
]}
</script>

<main class="lp-page saas-shortlist" id="simple-guide">
  <div class="lp-hero-shell"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <nav class="lp-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/resources/outbound-sales-library/">Outbound Sales Library</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">SaaS appointment setting companies</span></nav>
    <div class="lp-hero">
      <div>
        <h1>5 Best SaaS Appointment Setting Companies to Hire in 2027</h1>
        <p class="lp-intro">Compare five providers for B2B software demos. See what they charge, who they reach and what your sales team receives.</p>
        <div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-button" href="#comparison">Compare providers ↓</a><a class="lp-text-link" href="#callteam-proof">See CallTeam’s demo campaign ↓</a></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="lp-brief saas-shortlist-brief" aria-labelledby="saas-buy-for">
        <h2 id="saas-buy-for">Our pick for phone-led SaaS demos</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>North America–based callers.</strong> We handle callbacks, leave live voicemails and use approved prerecorded voicemail drops.</li>
          <li><strong>From US$4,000 per month</strong> for managed calling, demo qualification and a CRM handoff.</li>
          <li><a href="#callteam-proof">See how we booked 11 qualified demos in 90 days →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div></div>

  <nav class="lp-jump" aria-label="On this page"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <a href="#comparison">Prices and fit</a><a href="#callteam-proof">CallTeam’s work</a><a href="#agency-reviews">Agency verdicts</a><a href="#demo-handoff">Sample handoff</a><a href="#quote-check">Questions to ask</a><a href="#questions">FAQs</a>
  </div></nav>

  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>Compare SaaS appointment setting providers</h2>
      <p>CallTeam publishes this guide and sells appointment setting. We checked provider pricing and scope on <time datetime="{{ shortlist.checkedDate }}">{{ shortlist.checkedLabel }}</time>. Prices use each provider’s published currency notation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap">
      <table class="lp-table sg-table saas-shortlist-table" role="table">
        <caption>Five agencies compared by buyer, outreach and published price</caption>
        <thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Provider</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Best fit</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Outreach and buyer examples</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Published price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for provider in shortlist.providers %}
          <tr role="row"{% if loop.first %} class="saas-shortlist-own-row"{% endif %}>
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader"><a href="#{{ provider.id }}">{{ provider.name }}</a></th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Best fit">{{ provider.fit }}</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Outreach and buyer examples">{{ provider.reach }}</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Published price"><strong>{{ provider.pricing }}</strong><small>{{ provider.pricingNote }}</small></td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="callteam-proof"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>How CallTeam booked demos for a real estate SaaS platform</h2>
      <p>Site-selection teams had to pull property and market data from several sources. Our callers asked where the research slowed down. Buyers agreed to see how the platform could help them compare locations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="saas-shortlist-evidence">
      {{ processVideoPreview('Watch CallTeam’s 78-second process demo', 'See how our callers qualify interest and brief your sales team.', 'saas-agency-shortlist') }}
      <div class="saas-shortlist-results">
        <h3>What the campaign produced</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Qualified demos booked in 90 days</dt><dd>11</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Sales opportunities</dt><dd>4</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Customers within six months</dt><dd>2</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <a href="/case-studies/saas-demo-appointment-setting/">Read the SaaS campaign case study →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="agency-reviews"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>How each agency qualifies and hands off SaaS demos</h2>
    </div>
    {% for provider in shortlist.providers %}
      <article class="lp-provider saas-shortlist-review" id="{{ provider.id }}">
        <header class="lp-provider-head"><h3>{{ provider.name }}</h3><p>{{ provider.headline }}</p></header>
        <div class="lp-provider-body">
          <div class="lp-provider-detail">
            <h4>How they qualify</h4><p>{{ provider.qualification }}</p>
            <h4>What goes to sales</h4><p>{{ provider.handoff }}</p>
          </div>
          <aside class="lp-verdict"><h4>Buying verdict</h4><p>{{ provider.verdict }}</p>{% if provider.check %}<p>{{ provider.check }}</p>{% endif %}</aside>
        </div>
        <ul class="saas-shortlist-sources" aria-label="{{ provider.name }} sources">
          {% for source in provider.sources %}<li><a href="{{ source[1] }}">{{ source[0] }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="demo-handoff"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>What a qualified SaaS demo looks like in the CRM</h2>
      <p>Ask for a sample CRM note before you sign. It should give your rep enough context to prepare the demo.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-two saas-shortlist-handoff">
      <div>
        <h3>An access approval software demo</h3>
        <p>Sample CRM handoff</p>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Buyer</dt><dd>IT operations manager at a 450-person company. Owns employee access requests.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Problem</dt><dd>Managers approve access in chat. IT chases approvals and keeps audit records by hand.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Demo purpose</dt><dd>Show how the platform routes an approval and exports the audit trail.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Open question</dt><dd>Single sign-on is required. Confirm the identity provider before the call.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Next step</dt><dd>The buyer accepted the invite and will ask the security lead to join.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Track the three outcomes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Booked.</strong> The buyer agreed to the meeting.</li>
          <li><strong>Held.</strong> The buyer attended.</li>
          <li><strong>Sales-accepted.</strong> Your rep confirmed the account and use case met the agreed criteria.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Use the same rules for each provider so you can compare meeting quality.</p>
        <a class="lp-text-link" href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Use the Meeting Quality Check →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="quote-check"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>Five questions to send every agency</h2></div>
    <div class="sg-resource">
      <pre id="sg-resource-text" tabindex="-1">{% for question in shortlist.quoteQuestions %}{{ loop.index }}. {{ question }}{% if not loop.last %}{{ "\n" }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}</pre>
      <button class="lp-button" type="button" id="sg-copy-resource" hidden>Copy the five questions</button>
      <p id="sg-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-text-link" href="/lead-generation-proposal-comparison/">Compare agency quotes →</a><a class="lp-text-link" href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/b2b-saas-cold-call-script/">See our free SaaS cold call script →</a><a class="lp-text-link" href="/articles/b2b-appointment-setting-saas-companies/">Read the SaaS appointment setting playbook →</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="questions"><div class="lp-wrap lp-faq-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>SaaS appointment setting FAQs</h2></div>
    <div class="lp-faqs">{% for faq in shortlist.faqs %}<details><summary>{{ faq.question }}</summary><p>{{ faq.answer }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section saas-shortlist-close"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>Talk to CallTeam about booking SaaS demos</h2>
      <p>Tell us what you sell and who buys it. We’ll scope the campaign and show what sales gets before each demo.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-booking-placement="saas-agency-shortlist">Book a free 30-minute call ↗</a><a class="lp-text-link" href="/services/saas-appointment-setting/">Explore our SaaS appointment setting service →</a></div>
  </div></section>
</main>
